How can I implement a function in Swift that calculates the Environmental Sustainability Index (ESI) taking into account both socio-economic factors and environmental indicators? How can this function be utilized to assess policies and guarantee a fair allocation of resources while dealing with climate change and possible trade-offs? 
[Swift code]:
func calculateESI(socioEcoFactors: [Double], envIndicators: [Double]) -> Double {
  let totalSocioEco = socioEcoFactors.reduce(0, +)
  let totalEnvIndicators = envIndicators.reduce(0, +)
  let avgSocioEco = totalSocioEco / Double(socioEcoFactors.count)
  let avgEnvIndicators = totalEnvIndicators / Double(envIndicators.count)
  let esi = (avgSocioEco + avgEnvIndicators) / 2.0
  return esi
}
