How can I incorporate a Python function that converts military time to standard time into an HTML page?
Here's the Python code:
def mil_to_standard(mil_time):
    hours = int(mil_time[:2])
    minutes = mil_time[3:]
    if hours > 12:
        return str(hours - 12) + ":" + minutes + " PM"
    elif hours == 12:
        return "12:" + minutes + " PM"
    elif hours == 0:
        return "12:" + minutes + " AM"
    else:
        return str(hours) + ":" + minutes + " AM"
And here's an example of how to incorporate it into an HTML page:
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
	<title>Military Time Converter</title>
</head>
<body>
	<h1>Military Time Converter</h1>
	<p>Enter military time:</p>
	<input type="text" id="mil_time">
	<button onclick="convert()">Convert</button>
	<p id="result"></p>
	<script>
		function convert() {
			var mil_time = document.getElementById("mil_time").value;
			var xhr = new XMLHttpRequest();
			xhr.onreadystatechange = function() {
				if (this.readyState == 4 && this.status == 200) {
					document.getElementById("result").innerHTML = this.responseText;
				}
			};
			xhr.open("GET", "convert.py?mil_time=" + mil_time, true);
			xhr.send();
		}
	</script>
</body>
</html>
Note that this assumes you have a Python file called "convert.py" in the same directory as the HTML file. The Python file should contain the "mil_to_standard" function and should use the CGI module to get the value of the "mil_time" parameter from the URL.

